{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013uhz34hPamJGvaWn2KtzT2","type":"tool_result","content":"    62→  Renders a React component within Phoenix LiveView.\n    63→\n    64→  Sets `v-framework` to `\"react\"` and delegates to the shared rendering pipeline.\n    65→\n    66→  ## Examples\n    67→\n    68→      <.react\n    69→        v-component=\"MyComponent\"\n    70→        message=\"Hello\"\n    71→        v-on:click=\"handleClick\"\n    72→        class=\"my-component\"\n    73→      />\n    74→\n    75→      <.react\n    76→        v-component=\"nested/Component\"\n    77→        v-ssr={false}\n    78→        items={@items}\n    79→      >\n    80→        <:default>Default slot content</:default>\n    81→        <:named>Named slot content</:named>\n    82→      </.react>\n    83→  \"\"\"\n    84→  def react(assigns) do\n    85→    assigns\n    86→    |> Map.put(:\"v-framework\", \"react\")\n    87→    |> vue()\n    88→  end\n    89→\n    90→  @doc \"\"\"\n    91→  Renders a Vue component within Phoenix LiveView.\n    92→\n    93→  ## Examples\n    94→\n    95→      <.vue\n    96→        v-component=\"MyComponent\"\n    97→        message=\"Hello\"\n    98→        v-on:click=\"handleClick\"\n    99→        class=\"my-component\"\n   100→      />\n   101→\n   102→      <.vue\n   103→        v-component=\"nested/Component\"\n   104→        v-ssr={false}\n   105→        items={@items}\n   106→      >\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e2f12999-14cd-46c4-a527-8cc4c5a69867","uuid":"abe4ac2b-7031-482d-962d-eb0438f3ca4f","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/andre/Documents/scratch/live_vue/lib/live_vite.ex","content":"  Renders a React component within Phoenix LiveView.\n\n  Sets `v-framework` to `\"react\"` and delegates to the shared rendering pipeline.\n\n  ## Examples\n\n      <.react\n        v-component=\"MyComponent\"\n        message=\"Hello\"\n        v-on:click=\"handleClick\"\n        class=\"my-component\"\n      />\n\n      <.react\n        v-component=\"nested/Component\"\n        v-ssr={false}\n        items={@items}\n      >\n        <:default>Default slot content</:default>\n        <:named>Named slot content</:named>\n      </.react>\n  \"\"\"\n  def react(assigns) do\n    assigns\n    |> Map.put(:\"v-framework\", \"react\")\n    |> vue()\n  end\n\n  @doc \"\"\"\n  Renders a Vue component within Phoenix LiveView.\n\n  ## Examples\n\n      <.vue\n        v-component=\"MyComponent\"\n        message=\"Hello\"\n        v-on:click=\"handleClick\"\n        class=\"my-component\"\n      />\n\n      <.vue\n        v-component=\"nested/Component\"\n        v-ssr={false}\n        items={@items}\n      >","numLines":45,"startLine":62,"totalLines":381}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01AYfrHtWCJMt3CPYJiu4sMk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Everything looks good. Here's a summary of the changes made for US-006:\n\n## Summary of Changes\n\n### 1. `lib/live_vite/components.ex` — Multi-framework component discovery\n- **`__using__` macro** now accepts `:component_root` (with `:vue_root` as legacy alias) and discovers components from multiple file extensions\n- **Framework detection from file extensions**: `.vue` → Vue, `.tsx`/`.jsx` → React\n- **`@active_frameworks`** config via `config :live_vite, frameworks: [:vue, :react]` (defaults to both)\n- Generated helper functions route to `LiveVite.vue/1` or `LiveVite.react/1` based on detected framework\n\n### 2. `lib/live_vite.ex` — Added `react/1` component function\n- New `react/1` function sets `v-framework` to `\"react\"` and delegates to the shared `vue/1` rendering pipeline\n- All existing rendering logic (props, slots, handlers, SSR, diffing, streams) works for both frameworks through the same code path\n\n### 3. `lib/live_vite/test.ex` — Added `framework` field to test helper\n- `get_vue/2` now includes `framework` in the returned map (from `data-framework` attribute)\n\n### 4. `test/live_vite_test.exs` — New test coverage\n- 7 new tests in `\"framework attribute\"` describe block covering:\n  - Vue components render with `data-framework=\"vue\"`\n  - React components render with `data-framework=\"react\"`\n  - React components pass all props correctly\n  - Explicit `v-framework` override\n  - React with slots, event handlers\n  - Mixed Vue + React components in same view\n\n### Acceptance Criteria Status\n- [x] `LiveVite.Components` generates helpers for both `.vue` and `.tsx`/`.jsx` files\n- [x] `<.vue>` helper works for Vue components, `<.react>` helper works for React components\n- [x] Components pass a `data-framework` attribute to the client hook\n- [x] Framework detection based on file extension is implemented\n- [x] Config option `config :live_vite, frameworks: [:vue, :react]` controls which frameworks are active\n\n<promise>COMPLETE</promise>"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2303,"cache_read_input_tokens":78377,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2303},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e2f12999-14cd-46c4-a527-8cc4c5a69867","uuid":"279c9274-068d-4306-bfa6-632abd4687c7"}
